        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>The function <span class=\"math\">[MATH: g]</span> is defined by <span class=\"math\">[MATH: g(x) = 2x^{3} - 4.]</span> What is the value of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: g(-2)?]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "The function [MATH: g] is defined by [MATH: g(x) = 2x^{3} - 4.] What is the value of [MATH: g(-2)?]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>To find <span class=\"math\">[MATH: g(-2),]</span> we substitute <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x = -2]</span> into the function&#x27;s definition and evaluate:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: g(x)|= 2x^{3} \u2212 4; g(\u2212 2)|= 2(\u2212 2)^{3} \u2212 4; = 2 \u22c5 (\u2212 8) \u2212 4; = \u2212 16 \u2212 4; = \u2212 20]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "To find [MATH: g(-2),] we substitute [MATH: x = -2] into the function's definition and evaluate:\n\n[MATH: g(x)|= 2x^{3} \u2212 4; g(\u2212 2)|= 2(\u2212 2)^{3} \u2212 4; = 2 \u22c5 (\u2212 8) \u2212 4; = \u2212 16 \u2212 4; = \u2212 20]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nThe function [MATH: g] is defined by [MATH: g(x) = 2x^{3} - 4.] What is the value of [MATH: g(-2)?]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nTo find [MATH: g(-2),] we substitute [MATH: x = -2] into the function's definition and evaluate:\n\n[MATH: g(x)|= 2x^{3} \u2212 4; g(\u2212 2)|= 2(\u2212 2)^{3} \u2212 4; = 2 \u22c5 (\u2212 8) \u2212 4; = \u2212 16 \u2212 4; = \u2212 20]"
      },
